### PeerConnect API: manual tests
### VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each block.
### Start the server first: npm run dev
### Cookies are remembered between requests, so log in once and the rest work.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5001

### Health check (should show "database": "connected")
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

### ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Sign up (change the email each time, or use Login below)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Asha Verma",
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Log in
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "asha@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### Who am I? (session restore)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/check

### Socket token (used by the frontend for the Socket.IO handshake)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/socket-token

### Update name
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/update-profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Asha V."
}

### ── Messages ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Contacts (copy another user's _id from here for the requests below)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/messages/users

### Conversation history (replace the id)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/messages/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID?limit=30

### Send a message (replace the id; clientMessageId must be a new UUID each time)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/messages/send/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Hello from REST Client!",
  "clientMessageId": "{{$guid}}"
}

### ── Error cases ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Invalid signup → 400 with field details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "A",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Protected route without a session → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/messages/users
